   Changes made here: updated for official changes after 2017 (Eyüp renamed
   Eyüpsultan; new districts Sultanhanı/Aksaray and Kemalpaşa/Artvin in 2017
   and Derecik/Hakkari in 2018), spellings aligned with official forms
   (Hadim, 19 Mayıs, Marmaraereğlisi), central districts of non-metropolitan
   provinces named "Merkez", plate codes, regions and metropolitan flags added.
   Every province's district set was cross-checked against independent public
   lists; the total (973) matches the Ministry of Interior inventory.

2) src/data/dini-bayramlar.ts — Ramazan and Kurban Bayramı dates, 2024–2030

   Dates taken from the Diyanet İşleri Başkanlığı "Dini Günler" calendars
   (https://vakithesaplama.diyanet.gov.tr/dini_gunler.php). Calendar dates are
   facts; only the first day of each holiday is stored.

3) src/data/banka-kodlari.ts — bank / payment institution codes for IBAN labels

   Participant codes and names from the TCMB "FAST Sistem Katılımcıları" page
   (https://www.tcmb.gov.tr/wps/wcm/connect/fast/katilimcilar). Used only to
   label the bank code of a checksum-validated IBAN.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Live data (fetched at runtime, not bundled)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- TCMB indicative exchange rates: https://www.tcmb.gov.tr/kurlar/today.xml and
  the dated archive https://www.tcmb.gov.tr/kurlar/YYYYMM/DDMMYYYY.xml
- Resmî Gazete open data (MIT, by the same author), compiled from the official
  daily index: https://demiralpozturk.github.io/resmi-gazete-takip/
  This server does not scrape resmigazete.gov.tr.
- Supermarket prices open data (MIT, by the same author), derived from the
  Ministry of Trade's marketfiyati.org.tr store-level prices:
  https://demiralpozturk.github.io/market-scraper/products_data.json
  This server does not call marketfiyati.org.tr.

Test fixtures under test/fixtures are trimmed copies of responses from the
sources above, kept only for offline unit tests.
